# Citation File Format 1.2.0 — https://citation-file-format.github.io
#
# GitHub reads this file and offers a "Cite this repository" button. It exists
# because this project's output is largely measurements (MEASURED.md,
# BENCHMARK.md, LATENCY-150.md), and a measurement people can cite is worth
# more than one they cannot.
#
# `license:` below carries the SPDX identifier for the open-source half only,
# because SPDX has no identifier for the commercial half. Tokkah is dual
# licensed: AGPL-3.0-only for everyone, plus a separate commercial license
# (LICENSE-COMMERCIAL.md) for closed-source use. Cite the AGPL one.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use Tokkah, or reuse any of its measurements, please cite it using the
  metadata below.
title: Tokkah
abstract: >-
  Peer-to-peer video calling that sends bit-exact lossless 48 kHz PCM audio
  rather than a lossy codec, repairs lost packets with a sliding-window FEC,
  and paces video against the display's real refresh rate. Signaling is a
  single Cloudflare Worker and one Durable Object; media never touches a
  server. The flagship client is Kin, a native macOS application. Every
  performance claim in the repository is accompanied by the measurement that
  produced it, including the experiments that failed.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Devesh
    family-names: Patel
repository-code: "https://github.com/deshmukhpatel98/tokkah"
url: "https://room.tokkah.com"
license: AGPL-3.0-only
version: 0.69.0
date-released: "2026-08-26"
keywords:
  - video-calling
  - webrtc
  - lossless-audio
  - low-latency
  - forward-error-correction
  - real-time-communication
  - macos
  - swift
  - cloudflare-workers
